        "vraag": "Classify these movements with Aberle's four types and explain your choice: (a) a mindfulness network promoting personal inner peace; (b) a campaign for a law requiring gender-neutral toilets in all public buildings; (c) an extremist group that wants to replace democracy with a religious state; (d) a sect that demands a complete change of life from its new members.",
        "antwoord": "**(a) Alternative**: limited change, in specific individuals who choose to join; not openly political.\n\n**(b) Reformative**: limited change (one law), but it affects **everyone**, and it works inside the political system.\n\n**(c) Revolutionary**: it wants the **basic transformation** of society for everyone and rejects existing institutions.\n\n**(d) Redemptive**: radical change, but only in the **individuals** it recruits, through conversion."
